# Synthetic walkthrough; replace returned identifiers and sessions as you go.
# Open in an HTTP client supporting .http variables, or translate to curl/Postman.
# Google exchange requires a real credential with this challenge's nonce.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@frontendOrigin = http://localhost:5173
@ownerToken = REPLACE_WITH_OWNER_APP_SESSION
@memberToken = REPLACE_WITH_MEMBER_APP_SESSION
@workspaceId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003
@boardId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004
@taskId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006
@invitationId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008
@memberId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

### Obtain a challenge. Use nonce in GIS; do not submit the placeholder credential below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/google/challenges
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}

### Exchange the real Google credential; repeat sign-in separately for the member.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/google/exchange
Origin: {{frontendOrigin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"challenge_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013","id_token":"REPLACE_WITH_REAL_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN"}

### Owner creates workspace. Update workspaceId with returned id.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

{"name":"DevOps Team"}

### Owner invites an already registered member. Update invitationId.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

{"email":"dara@example.com"}

### Member accepts.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/invitations/{{invitationId}}/response
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"accept"}

### Create board. Update boardId from response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/boards
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003

{"name":"Todo"}

### Inspect members; obtain the real memberId for assignment/mention.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### Create assigned task. Update taskId and retain response ETag.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004

{"board_id":"{{boardId}}","title":"Build task service","assignee_id":"{{memberId}}","start_date":"2026-11-15","due_date":"2026-11-20"}

### Add a mention. Offsets count Unicode code points; @Dara starts at 14.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005

{"body":"Please review @Dara","mentions":[{"user_id":"{{memberId}}","start":14,"length":5}]}

### Read notifications after asynchronous delivery.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?unread_only=true&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

### Update task using current ETag, replacing "1" if it has changed.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{"description":"Implementation started."}

### Move uses PATCH {"board_id":"<another board in this workspace>"} and latest If-Match.
### Mark-read uses POST /api/v1/notifications/<returned-id>/read with no body.
### Sign out current member session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}
